Example: a holding bought before the report becomes its opening value.
Salary funds one FUND unit bought on 2022-12-31 at 100 USD; it closes at 100.
The report starts on 2023-01-01, so that previous close is opening value 100.
The quote rises to 110 USD on 2023-07-01 and 120 USD on 2024-01-01, with no
postings during the report interval. Net contributions are 0, and profit/loss
is 120 - 100 - 0 = 20 USD. Time-weighted return is 120 / 100 - 1 = 20%.
Treating the 100 USD opening value as invested for 365 days also gives a 20%
money-weighted return.

========== CLI ==========

ledlight investment-performance --accounts Assets:Fund --commodities FUND --from 2023-01-01 --to 2024-01-01 --format text

========== FILE ==========

commodity USD
  default
  format 1,000.00 USD
commodity FUND
  format 1,000 FUND
account Assets:Fund
account Assets:Cash
account Income:Salary
P 2022-12-31 FUND 100 USD
P 2023-07-01 FUND 110 USD
P 2024-01-01 FUND 120 USD

2022-12-31 Salary
  Assets:Cash  100 USD
  Income:Salary  -100 USD

2022-12-31 Purchase
  Assets:Fund  1 FUND {100 USD}
  Assets:Cash  -100 USD

========== OUTPUT ==========

Investment performance from 2023-01-01 to 2024-01-01
Instruments: 1
Opening value: 100.00 USD
Net contributions: 0.00 USD
Ending value: 120.00 USD
Profit/loss: 20.00 USD
Time-weighted return (total): 20.00 %
Time-weighted return (annualized): 20.00 %
Money-weighted return (total): 20.00 %
Money-weighted return (annualized): 20.00 %

========== WARNINGS ==========
